body:
@joelbernstein this is a friendly reminder to keep things professional; we abide by the CNCF Code of Conduct and we ask members to follow that code.

Regardless of whether or not Visual Studio injects improper code, if the maintenance burden on our end is minimal, we'd be open to PRs to alleviate that issue. If it's fixed upstream, then it's fixed and it is an effective no-op.

@NArnott would you be willing to take a closer look and see what would be required to support this functionality?
